# sha256 manifest for the VMAF model JSONs the worker image bundles
# (Dockerfile "VMAF models" layer). Source: Netflix/vmaf at commit
# 3f9e02af258a5c0e30124fc585a3c3af90126dee (= tag v3.2.0), hashes computed
# from an independent download on 2026-08-06. Verified in-image with
# `sha256sum -c --strict` right after the downloads — a tampered or
# truncated model fails the build (fail-closed), it can never ship.
# Filenames are relative to $VMAF_MODEL_DIR (the check cd's there first).
# The manifest is COPY'd to $VMAF_MODEL_DIR/vmaf-models.sha256 and kept in
# the image, so `cd $VMAF_MODEL_DIR && sha256sum -c vmaf-models.sha256`
# re-verifies the models inside a running container.
# When bumping VMAF_MODEL_REF: re-download, re-hash, update this file.
